  "text": "HAROLD J. LAWRENCE\nF.A.S.A.; M.INST.T.\nTRANSPORT CONSULTANT\nTELEPHONE: MU 3552: RESIDENCE. WF 2969\n405 COLLINS STREET.\nMELBOURNE. C.1.\nVICTORIA\n10th June, 1955.\nChas. E. McFadyen, Esq., C.B.E.,\nSecretary,\nDepartment of Shipping & Transport,\nRialto Building,\nCollins Street,\nMELBOURNE•\nDear Charles,\nPermit me to congratulate you very warmly on the high\nhonour which has been bestowed on you in the Queen's Birth-\nday Honours.\nThose of us who have worked with you and\nseen your worth over the years believe that the honour is\nvery well deserved.\nSincerely yours,\nStands\nTRANSPORT ACCOUNIING ••• LAXATION\n•ADVOGACY\nSURVEYS AND INVESTIGATIONS\nINDUSTRY SECRETARIAT\nCITIUS • ALTIUS • FORTIUS\nThe Chairman and Members of\nThe Oxecutive of the Organising\nfor the Olympic Games, Melbourne, 1956\nrequest the honour of the company of\nMs. CS Metadyen, C.%, and thas Shetadyew\nat The Solemn Opening of the Congross\nf the International Olympic Committee\nin the Melbourne Sown Halt\non Monduy, 191 November, 1956, at 11a.m.\nR. I.% I. by 17 t Soptember,\nto The Chief Executive Officer\nOlympic Games Committee, G. P.O.. Melbourne",
